  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything. The Stock API call needs a decision from you first.\n\n**The blocker is ARCH-5.** This service may only call systems the architecture catalog declares, and today that is only `payments-api`. `stock.inventory.internal` would be a new outbound dependency. It has to be declared in the catalog and approved by Architecture before the call ships. I couldn't find a catalog in this repo, so I can't check whether that has already happened. Your request tells me what you want, but it doesn't show that Architecture approved it.\n\n**What I'd build once that's cleared:**\n- **Port:** a `StockChecker` port in `src/core/ports.ts` (ARCH-1).\n- **Adapter:** `src/adapters/httpStockChecker.ts`, modelled on `httpPaymentGateway.ts`. It would call `GET /v1/stock/{sku}`, which is the only place the external call lives (ARCH-3).\n- **Service:** `orderService` checks every line before payment and saving, and throws a new `InsufficientStockError` if any line's quantity is more than `available`.\n- **Error mapping:** `errorMapper` turns `InsufficientStockError` into a 409.\n- **Wiring:** `createApp` gets an optional `stockChecker` dep, so the existing tests keep working.\n- **Tests:** cover the 409 case and the case where there is enough stock.\n\nI'd also like your call on these points:\n1. **Stock API unreachable:** should orders fail closed (503, like `PaymentUnavailableError`) or fail open and accept the order? I'd default to failing closed.\n2. **Default `stockChecker`:** when `createApp` gets none, I'd default to an always-available stub. That keeps the existing tests passing, but production wiring would need to supply the real adapter.\n3. **Duplicate SKUs:** if the same SKU appears on several lines, I'd sum the quantities before comparing. Say if you'd rather check each line separately.\n\n**How should I proceed?**\n- If Architecture has approved this, tell me where it's recorded (a ticket or catalog entry) and I'll implement it.\n- If it hasn't, I can still write the port, service logic, 409 mapping and tests, and leave the HTTP adapter out until approval.",
